Sat Aug 29 07:13:24 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.2.0:
  * Beta files and skills namespaces now use the GA response
    shapes; the dated beta header pins are gone
  * webhooks: unwrap() now requires the request headers to be
    passed explicitly
  * bedrock/aws: sign the raw request bytes so binary file
    uploads work
  * sessions: the event accumulator tolerates unknown event
    types instead of failing on them
  * tools: read() can return a view_range from a file larger
    than the size cap
  * tools: the agent toolset and memory tool preserve exact
    file bytes, no newline translation

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Aug 27 05:47:11 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.1.0:
  * Add the beta Organization API resources: organization users,
    invites, API keys, external keys, rate limits, service
    accounts, workspaces and federation
  * Add the "updates" thinking display mode to the beta adaptive
    thinking configuration
  * Add the anthropic-beta header values that were missing:
    compact, computer-use, mcp-tunnels, structured-outputs,
    task-budgets, thinking-display-updates and ce-user-management
  * Keep the beta tool runner going when a response stops with
    pause_turn or compaction instead of ending the turn
  * Fix the documentation link for the long-requests error

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Aug 21 05:38:01 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.0.0:
  * Switch the HTTP client from python-httpx to
    python-httpx2 >= 2.0.0; passing an httpx.Client now
    raises TypeError
  * Drop the python-distro runtime dependency
  * Raise the Python floor from 3.9 to 3.10
  * Remove the legacy Text Completions API
    (client.completions.create and HUMAN_PROMPT/AI_PROMPT)
  * .with_raw_response now returns APIResponse /
    AsyncAPIResponse (async parse/read/text/json are
    coroutines; .text and .content became methods)
  * Bedrock clients now require a region; unknown
    streaming events are skipped
  * Stop warning about output_format= on the parse,
    stream and tool_runner helpers
  * Vendor httpx_aiohttp under anthropic/_vendor;
    License is now MIT AND BSD-3-Clause
  * Ship MIGRATION.md as documentation

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Aug 20 05:46:46 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.125.0:
  * Promote Files and Skills APIs to GA and add computer-use
    and browser-use toolsets
  * Add helpers for reading the workspace ID in response headers
  * Add managed-agents web-search config and self-hosted sandbox
    memory-store sync
  * Extend files, memory stores, skills and user-profile APIs
  * Drop the unsupported mid_conv_system content block
  * Compute platform headers without spawning a subprocess
  * Export ServiceUnavailableError, DeadlineExceededError and
    custom status errors from the package
  * Retry session-runner tool-result sends for at least the
    lease TTL and run synchronous session tools in a worker
    thread

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Aug 14 07:29:53 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.122.0:
  * Add output_behavior to dream creation, selecting whether a new
    memory store is created or the input store is updated in place
  * Expose beta.messages.parse, stream and tool_runner on the
    Bedrock and Vertex clients
  * Run AWS SigV4 signing off the event loop in async clients
  * Treat an empty ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN as
    unset, and keep the token exchange bound per client across
    copy()
  * Read PathLike contents passed inside a file tuple
  * Fix several streaming accumulator bugs: apply all message_delta
    fields, keep omitted content block fields unset, emit
    input_json events for server tool use blocks and add context to
    malformed tool input JSON errors
  * Reject symlink loops in tool paths and skip special
    skill-archive members

